# The production build environment, in git on purpose.
#
# Every value here is public by construction: Astro compiles anything named `PUBLIC_*` into the
# browser bundle, so all of it is already readable by view-source on korczak.xyz. A Firebase web
# config is not a credential — the security boundary is firestore.rules plus Auth, not the
# obscurity of the API key — and the VAPID public key is the half of the pair designed to be
# handed to every subscriber. The private half is in Secret Manager and never comes near this file.
#
# Why committed rather than held in CI:
#
# These lived in the Netlify site's environment, and the failure that argues against that is on
# record — functions/README.md stated the VAPID key was set there, and it was, but only in the
# production context, so a plain `netlify env:list` showed six variables and no way to tell the
# seventh was missing rather than absent. A value that is invisible until it is wrong belongs in
# the repo, where a diff shows it changing.
#
# The failure mode is quiet, which is the other reason. None of these are required: src/lib/
# firebase.ts and useWebPush.ts both degrade to localStorage-only when they are unset, so a
# missing value does not break the build — it ships a site where login and push have silently
# stopped existing. Keeping them next to the code means a fresh clone builds the real site.
#
# Precedence, which is not the direction you would guess: Vite loads `.env` first and the
# mode-specific file second, so during `npm run build` this file OVERRIDES `.env`. Editing `.env`
# will not change a production build. `npm run dev` is the other way round — mode `development`
# never loads this file at all, so `.env` governs there. Use `.env.production.local` (gitignored)
# to point a local build somewhere else.

# Firebase web config — console > Project settings > General > Your apps > SDK setup.
PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyByJOvgDZd7Lb3WtcDDJjkTOkAAO6jmGV4
PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=korczak-xyz-501720.firebaseapp.com
PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=korczak-xyz-501720
PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=korczak-xyz-501720.firebasestorage.app
PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=1068962621574
PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:1068962621574:web:5f4592aad9fb50b9f00907

# Web Push (Event Watch). Rotating this silently invalidates every push subscription on
# every device, with no error anywhere — so it can never change. See functions/README.md.
PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=BGnkRSyA-RSvzD4zR7oy9mgRnFbY89roM9CiX6pESuwvrpF8qwmFg7Sv01mC7iRUVmZG65anvlHclL6K9DIHZAY
